# r1107tp boot a2: same save as a1 (restart), tools/scratch_query/ztp_probe.js copied in as zz_ztp_probe.js.
# Bot qa (perfBot) holds a Tempad in slot 0; locations "Home One" (0.5 -60 0.5), "Far East" (30.5 -60 0.5), "Hell Spot"
# (Nether 0.5 120 0.5) and pin "Far East" were made on a1 by hand (SQ-TP-04 log in the run doc).
# Rows SQ-TP-03 (restart half), -05, -07.
pace 1

## SQ-TP-03 | locations and Teleport app after a restart
bootexpect Done \(
> pbot spawn qa 0.5 -60 0.5 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> ztp locs qa
waitlog \[ztp\] done 20
expect \[ztp\] loc tempad:default .* "Home One" minecraft:overworld 0\.50 -60\.00 0\.50
expect \[ztp\] loc tempad:default .* "Far East" minecraft:overworld 30\.50
expect \[ztp\] loc tempad:default .* "Hell Spot" minecraft:the_nether 0\.50 120\.00
> pbot hold qa tempad:tempad
> zq useitem qa
> ztp menu qa
waitlog \[ztp\] menu 20
expect \[ztp\] menu tempad:teleport

## SQ-TP-05 | pinned location + default macro, after restart and after a death
> ztp pdata qa
waitlog \[ztp\] pdata 20
expect pinned_location:\{locationId:\[I;-191329597,-100384576,-1821537137,2007787117\],providerId:"tempad:default"\}
> ztp settings qa tempad:teleport tempad:default
> ztp setchr qa 0 6000
> kill @e[type=tempad:timedoor]
sleep 3
> ztp macro qa
> ztp doors
waitlog \[ztp\] doors total 20
expect \[ztp\] door minecraft:overworld .* target minecraft:overworld \(30\.5, -60\.0, 0\.5\)
> kill @e[type=tempad:timedoor]
> gamerule keepInventory true
> kill qa
sleep 3
> pbot spawn qa 0.5 -60 0.5 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 2
> ztp pdata qa
waitlog \[ztp\] pdata 20
count pinned_location:\{locationId:\[I;-191329597 >= 2
> ztp macro qa
> ztp doors
waitlog \[ztp\] doors total 20
count \[ztp\] door minecraft:overworld .* target minecraft:overworld \(30\.5, -60\.0, 0\.5\) >= 2
look perfBot relogs a dead bot (no PlayerEvent.Clone): the death half covers save/load only; Clone (copyFrom) needs a client death (CQ note)

## SQ-TP-07 | chronon generator charges a carried Tempad
> kill @e[type=tempad:timedoor]
> clear qa
> give qa tempad:tempad
> give qa tempad:chronon_generator
sleep 1
> ztp chr qa
waitlog \[ztp\] chr end 20
sleep 120
> ztp chr qa
waitlog \[ztp\] chr end 20
shell grep -hE "\[ztp\] chr slot" logs/latest.log | tail -6
look tempad chronons rose between the two chr reads (generator 1 per 48 ticks: about 50 in 2 min)
